1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,020
PatientKeeper Retorno helps a doctor keep the
next step visible when a

2
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:06,120
patient follow-up remains unfinished.

3
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:11,880
Created by Athos from Figueira, this
prototype grew from the scattered contacts

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:15,480
and incomplete follow-ups we see while
supporting medical practices.

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,400
All cases in this demonstration are
fictional.

6
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:23,020
The doctor workspace brings the journey,
consultation and contact history together.

7
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,260
Here, a fictional bunion and bunionette
surgery labels the scenario.

8
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:32,420
The doctor chooses the phase, the responsible
person, the next administrative action

9
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:33,340
and a check date.

10
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,440
The system does not invent surgical
instructions or clinical deadlines.

11
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:42,600
The practice receives an organized record
without requiring reception staff to operate

12
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,400
this demonstration.

13
00:00:43,979 --> 00:00:47,859
The local version really transcribes a
fictional audio file on this computer.

14
00:00:48,439 --> 00:00:52,959
Portuguese and English audio are supported
independently from the navigation language.

15
00:00:53,599 --> 00:00:57,739
The doctor reviews the original transcript
and selects literal segments to prepare

16
00:00:57,739 --> 00:00:59,159
a note with source references.

17
00:00:59,779 --> 00:01:01,079
This draft is an extraction,

18
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:05,099
not a model-generated clinical summary or a
signed medical record.

19
00:01:05,739 --> 00:01:08,299
Selecting a different file requires a new
declaration.

20
00:01:09,079 --> 00:01:11,939
Changing language or tabs preserves the
selected audio.

21
00:01:12,459 --> 00:01:16,099
The contact routine checks the recorded
preference and requires review of the

22
00:01:16,099 --> 00:01:18,119
exact administrative source and message.

23
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:22,599
The action shown here is a simulation: no
WhatsApp message is sent.

24
00:01:23,179 --> 00:01:25,379
A response and the next step remain visible.

25
00:01:25,879 --> 00:01:30,438
A refusal blocks further contact. Changing
the source invalidates the earlier review.

26
00:01:31,098 --> 00:01:33,758
A human records the administrative
resolution, so

27
00:01:33,758 --> 00:01:36,178
preparing a message alone cannot close the
episode.

28
00:01:36,778 --> 00:01:41,378
We also executed five distinct administrative
queries through the AMD Token Factory

29
00:01:41,378 --> 00:01:41,828
service.

30
00:01:42,558 --> 00:01:45,998
The official usage history maps the requested
Gemma model to the returned

31
00:01:45,998 --> 00:01:50,398
identifier. Three responses produced
candidates supported by literal citations.

32
00:01:51,058 --> 00:01:54,718
One response abstained when the essential
source was absent, and one request

33
00:01:54,718 --> 00:01:58,398
timed out. The final positive case ran
through the product API.

34
00:01:59,158 --> 00:02:02,618
These experiments used the follow-up queue,
not the new consultation note.

35
00:02:03,278 --> 00:02:06,438
The public panel displays recorded evidence
matched to the current question and

36
00:02:06,438 --> 00:02:08,698
sources; it does not start live inference.

37
00:02:09,289 --> 00:02:14,109
A clinical question, conflicting records, or
changed context blocks reuse of an

38
00:02:14,109 --> 00:02:14,589
old answer.

39
00:02:15,269 --> 00:02:19,349
The original queue, fictional doctor
calendar, English, Portuguese and Spanish

40
00:02:19,349 --> 00:02:22,309
navigation, and light and dark appearance
remain available.

41
00:02:23,189 --> 00:02:25,329
Gemma runs on the AMD service.

42
00:02:26,009 --> 00:02:28,229
Audio transcription runs locally on the CPU.

43
00:02:29,029 --> 00:02:32,409
The public static version cannot transcribe
audio or send messages.

44
00:02:33,049 --> 00:02:36,649
This separation makes the limits visible
instead of presenting a prepared action

45
00:02:36,649 --> 00:02:37,909
as an executed one.

46
00:02:37,909 --> 00:02:42,709
The intended value is fewer unfinished
follow-ups and less repeated administrative

47
00:02:42,709 --> 00:02:43,189
work.

48
00:02:43,829 --> 00:02:46,469
We have tested the software and the synthetic
workflow;

49
00:02:47,109 --> 00:02:49,909
operational savings and clinical outcomes
have not been measured.

50
00:02:50,649 --> 00:02:53,589
The administrative scaffold existed before
the event and is declared.

51
00:02:54,289 --> 00:02:58,769
Source review, real AMD experiments, and the
new doctor workspace were added

52
00:02:58,769 --> 00:02:59,469
during the event.

53
00:03:00,109 --> 00:03:04,129
The public demo and repository let judges
inspect the prototype, the source,

54
00:03:04,609 --> 00:03:05,569
and the recorded evidence.

55
00:03:05,569 --> 00:03:11,409
PatientKeeper Retorno: a source, a review,
and a next step.
